# The Jolly Balloon Man copying a transformed Delver of Secrets (CR 707.8, 707.9d): the copy's values are Insectile
# Aberration's, whose blue is its color indicator. "Red in addition to its other colors" provides a value for color, so the
# indicator is not copied, and the face has no mana cost: the token is red alone, while the original stays blue. Delver
# reveals Lightning Bolt at Bot1's turn-3 upkeep to transform; Jolly was cast on turn 1 so it can tap on turn 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Delver of Secrets
The Jolly Balloon Man
Island
Lightning Bolt
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Delver of Secrets.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Jolly Balloon Man.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.The Jolly Balloon Man.Activate(Insectile Aberration)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Insectile Aberration#1.Colors = Blue
Bot1.Battlefield.Insectile Aberration#2.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Insectile Aberration#2.Colors = Red
Bot1.Battlefield.Insectile Aberration#2.Power = 1
